# The legacy-um rule "allow netdomain self:icmp_socket create_socket_perms;"
# was removed here rather than narrowed.
#
# It is a stale duplicate of a platform rule that already exists, at
# system/sepolicy/private/net.te:30:
#
#   allow { netdomain -pcc_component } self:{ icmp_socket udp_socket rawip_socket } create_socket_perms;
#
# The platform grants this permission with pcc_component already excluded, as
# part of Android 17's tightening around pcc_component. The legacy-um copy
# predates that and has no exclusion, so it reached pcc_component - which
# carries net_domain() at system/sepolicy/private/pcc_component.te:10 - and
# tripped the neverallow at pcc_component.te:366:
#
#   (neverallow pcc_component pcc_component
#      { icmp_socket udp_socket rawip_socket } create_socket_perms)
#
# Deleting the duplicate loses nothing: every netdomain domain except
# pcc_component still gets the permission, from the platform rule. And the
# exclusion cannot be expressed here instead, because pcc_component is declared
# in system/sepolicy/private and is not exported to vendor policy, so
# checkpolicy rejects it as an unknown type when vendor_sepolicy.conf is built
# on its own.
#
# Upstream lineage-24.0-legacy-um at 33df3b661808 still carries the stale rule,
# so there is nothing to pull instead. A Gerrit change for this deletion should
# go to LineageOS/android_device_qcom_sepolicy_vndr.
